# 🌍 Life Expectancy Prediction Using Machine Learning

## 📌 Project Overview

This project aims to build a machine learning regression model capable of predicting **life expectancy** using demographic, economic, and health-related indicators collected by the World Health Organization (WHO).

The project follows a complete data science workflow—from data cleaning and exploratory data analysis (EDA) to feature engineering, feature selection, model building, evaluation, and interpretation.

This project was developed as a learning project to strengthen my understanding of regression analysis and the end-to-end machine learning pipeline.

---

## 🎯 Objectives

* Understand the factors influencing life expectancy.
* Build a regression model to predict life expectancy.
* Learn and apply best practices in data preprocessing.
* Compare different regression algorithms.
* Evaluate model performance using appropriate regression metrics.

---

## 📂 Dataset

**Dataset:** WHO Life Expectancy Dataset

The dataset contains health, economic, and social indicators collected from multiple countries over several years.

### Target Variable

* **Life expectancy** (years)

### Example Features

* Adult Mortality
* Infant Deaths
* Alcohol Consumption
* Percentage Expenditure
* Hepatitis B Immunization
* Measles Cases
* BMI
* Under-five Deaths
* Polio Immunization
* Total Expenditure
* Diphtheria Immunization
* HIV/AIDS
* GDP
* Population
* Thinness (1–19 years)
* Thinness (5–9 years)
* Income Composition of Resources
* Schooling
* Country
* Status (Developed / Developing)
* Year

---

## 🛠 Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Scikit-learn
* Jupyter Notebook

---

## 📊 Project Workflow

### 1. Data Loading

* Imported dataset
* Checked data types
* Explored dataset structure

### 2. Data Cleaning

* Removed missing target values
* Identified missing values in predictor variables
* Imputed missing values using appropriate strategies
* Checked for duplicate records

### 3. Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)

Performed:

* Summary statistics
* Distribution analysis
* Outlier detection
* Correlation analysis
* Feature relationship analysis

Visualizations included:

* Histograms
* Boxplots
* Correlation heatmap
* Scatter plots
* Bar charts

---

## ⚙ Feature Engineering

* Encoded categorical variables
* Investigated feature distributions
* Treated skewed variables where appropriate
* Prepared features for machine learning

---

## 🎯 Feature Selection

Feature selection was performed using:

* Correlation analysis
* Variance Inflation Factor (VIF)
* Recursive Feature Elimination (RFE)

These techniques helped identify the most informative variables while reducing multicollinearity.

---

## 🤖 Machine Learning Models

Models explored include:

* Linear Regression
* Ridge Regression
* Lasso Regression
* Decision Tree Regressor
* Random Forest Regressor

---

## 📈 Model Evaluation

Regression models were evaluated using:

* MAE (Mean Absolute Error)
* MSE (Mean Squared Error)
* RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)
* R² Score

---

